# Code owners for bevy-flock.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the base branch of a pull request, so it has to be on `main`
# before it can gate a review. Both accounts listed below have write access.
#
# The one rule this encodes: a pull request needs one approving review, and the author cannot
# approve their own pull request. Naming both accounts on the catch-all rule makes that
# explicit. A change opened by one account is reviewed by the other, and either account can open
# one, so the rule works in both directions without anyone being able to approve their own work.
#
# A pattern that names two owners means "one of these owners has to approve", not "both have to
# approve". Listing both is what keeps either account able to open a change.

